From bcb044937dc150471b6414589c3db836f78cb29c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 18:44:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebuild site around web design and video editing

Removes the thumbnail-design service entirely and repositions the site on the
two services that remain: web design/development and video editing.

Content
- Drops the thumbnail packages, the thumbnail portfolio grid, the skills bars,
  and the three thumbnail-related testimonials.
- Keeps the ten web strategy articles; removes the 34 thumbnail articles.
- Rewrites About around the engineering background and the channel that taught
  the editing and web work, with no thumbnail origin story.
- No pricing anywhere: services are scoped and quoted per project.
- Video work links to Fiverr/Upwork profiles rather than claiming a public reel.
  Both URLs are empty in the CONFIG block; while empty the site shows an email
  CTA instead of a dead button.

Rebuild
- New token-based design system with a dark and a light theme, persisted in
  localStorage and set before first paint so there is no flash.
- Space Grotesk / Inter / JetBrains Mono replace Bebas Neue + DM Sans.
- Drops the three.js CDN dependency; the hero is now a ~60-line canvas that
  pauses when hidden or off screen and is disabled under reduced motion.
- Drops the custom cursor and the percentage skill bars.
- Routes are now home/work/services/about/articles/contact, with the old
  /website, /reviews, /portfolio and /packages paths redirecting rather than
  breaking. Articles are deep-linkable at /articles/<slug>.
- Splits the single 174KB index.html into markup, stylesheet, article data and
  app logic under assets/.
- Adds skip link, focus-visible styles, focus trapping in the article modal,
  aria-current on the active nav item, reduced-motion and print handling.
- Adds .nojekyll, robots.txt, sitemap.xml and JSON-LD; the contact form now
  falls back to showing the email address when the request fails.
- Removes the unused victor-vandi-portfolio.html and the duplicate profile
  image whose filename contained a space.

